  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=-\\frac{4}{3},$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$   are\n\n$x\u2248$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{3}{4})={(-48.590\\,377\u2026)}^{\u2218}\u2248-{48.5904}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{48.5904}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={311.4096}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={311.4096}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={48.5904}^{\u2218}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={48.5904}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/d319d2ea403460a3b4d86c837a560fd5188476c425399145bb911e1414b0a6f5.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{\u2218}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{\u2218}+{48.5904}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u2248{228.5904}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx\u2248{228.6}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248{311.4}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
